.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt RELAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm relay
.Nd run a-Shell commands over authenticated HTTPS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm on | off | status | tokens | help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
controls an optional HTTPS server for executing commands from another
computer.
It is off by default and initially binds only to loopback.
Commands run serially.
Each request gets a fresh, noninteractive a-Shell session, starting in
Documents unless the
.Li X-Cwd
request header selects another directory, with standard input connected to
.Pa /dev/null .
The server returns command output and exit status as JSON; it does not share
the terminal screen or keyboard.
Keep a-Shell in the foreground: iOS can suspend it in the background.
.Pp
TLS and an
.Li X-Token
header are always required.
Mutual TLS is enabled by default and also requires a client certificate signed
by an enrolled CA.
.Bl -tag -width status
.It Cm on
Start or restart the listener using the saved configuration and enable
autostart at the next app launch.
Invalid configuration or missing client CA enrollment prevents startup.
If the configuration cannot be read, a running listener keeps its previous
settings; a failure after it has stopped can leave it stopped.
.It Cm off
Stop the listener and disable autostart.
Close connections and discard queued requests.
A command already running continues, subject to the output limit.
If the configuration is invalid, the listener still stops but the saved
autostart setting is unchanged.
.It Cm status
Show the listener state, saved autostart setting, configuration path,
effective settings, certificate fingerprints and a Mac curl command.
Create the default configuration with a random token if it does not exist.
When stopped, show the saved configuration.
With mutual TLS disabled, this output includes the token: keep it private.
If the saved configuration is invalid, report the error even while the
listener is running.
.It Cm tokens
Print the token for use in the Mac's
.Ev RELAY_TOKEN
environment variable.
Treat this output as a credential.
This is the saved token; after editing it, run
.Cm on
before using it.
.It Cm help
Print usage.
Invoking
.Nm
without an argument, or with
.Fl h
or
.Fl Fl help ,
also prints usage.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Run
.Dl relay status
then edit
.Pa ~/Documents/.relay.json .
Keep all five required fields:
.Bl -tag -width mutualTLS
.It Li enabled
Boolean, initially false.
Controls autostart;
.Cm on
and
.Cm off
update it.
.It Li bind
Numeric IPv4 or IPv6 address, initially
.Li 127.0.0.1 .
Use
.Li 0.0.0.0
for IPv4 access from a Mac, or
.Li ::
for IPv6.
.It Li port
TCP port, initially 8765 in full a-Shell or 8766 in mini and noPython.
Zero selects an available port; check
.Cm status
for the actual port.
.It Li mutualTLS
Boolean, initially true.
Requires
.Pa .relay-client-ca.der
in Documents.
Setting it to false removes the client certificate requirement; HTTPS and the
token remain required.
.It Li token
Random token generated on first configuration load.
Must contain 32 to 256 printable ASCII characters without spaces.
.El
.Pp
Changes take effect on
.Cm on
or the next app launch.
.Sh CONNECTING FROM A MAC
The following steps use mutual TLS and port 8765.
For other installations, replace both occurrences of 8765 in the curl
example with the port shown by
.Cm status .
The Mac needs curl and OpenSSL 3 or later; check
.Dl openssl version
before running the certificate commands.
The LibreSSL supplied by macOS is not OpenSSL 3.
If that is what the command reports, put an OpenSSL 3 installation's
.Pa bin
directory first in
.Ev PATH
and check the version again before continuing.
.Bl -enum
.It
In a-Shell, run
.Dl relay status
to create the configuration.
Change only the
.Li bind
value to
.Li 0.0.0.0
in
.Pa ~/Documents/.relay.json
and keep
.Li mutualTLS
true.
.It
On the Mac, open a new terminal window and use a private working directory.
Create a client CA and client certificate there;
.Li umask 077
remains in effect in that shell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
umask 077
openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes \e
    -keyout client-ca.key -out client-ca.pem -days 365 \e
    -subj '/CN=relay client CA' \e
    -addext 'basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE' \e
    -addext 'keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign'
openssl req -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes \e
    -keyout client.key -out client.csr \e
    -subj '/CN=relay Mac client'
printf '%s\en' 'basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE' \e
    'extendedKeyUsage=clientAuth' \e
    'keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature' > client.ext
openssl x509 -req -in client.csr -CA client-ca.pem \e
    -CAkey client-ca.key -CAcreateserial -out client.pem \e
    -days 365 -extfile client.ext
openssl x509 -in client-ca.pem -outform DER \e
    -out .relay-client-ca.der
.Ed
Keep both private keys on the Mac.
Anyone with the CA private key can issue another trusted client certificate.
.It
Copy only the public
.Pa .relay-client-ca.der
to a-Shell's Documents through a trusted channel such as USB file sharing.
Command-Shift-period shows hidden files in Finder.
In a-Shell, run:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
relay on
relay status
.Ed
The first successful setup creates a server identity and exports its public
certificate.
Copy
.Pa .relay-cert.pem
from Documents to the Mac's working directory through the trusted channel.
Keep the private
.Pa .relay-identity.p12
on the phone.
Compare the server certificate fingerprint on the Mac with the
.Li server certificate SHA-256
line from
.Cm status ,
and the CA fingerprint with its
.Li client CA SHA-256
line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openssl x509 -in .relay-cert.pem -noout -fingerprint -sha256
openssl x509 -in client-ca.pem -noout -fingerprint -sha256
.Ed
.It
Run
.Dl relay tokens
in a-Shell.
Set the Mac's
.Ev RELAY_TOKEN
to that value without saving it in shell history, a script or a URL.
For example, in the Mac's default zsh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
read -rs 'RELAY_TOKEN?Relay token: '; echo
export RELAY_TOKEN
.Ed
.It
Keep a-Shell open in the foreground.
Replace the documentation address
.Li 192.0.2.1
below with the phone's reachable Wi-Fi address.
The
.Cm status
output also supplies a curl command using that address when available:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl --cacert .relay-cert.pem --cert client.pem \e
    --key client.key \e
    --resolve 'relay.local:8765:192.0.2.1' \e
    -H "X-Token: $RELAY_TOKEN" --data-binary 'pwd' \e
    https://relay.local:8765/run
.Ed
The certificate names
.Li relay.local ;
.Fl -resolve
connects to the phone while retaining certificate name verification.
Trust the copied server certificate with
.Fl -cacert ;
do not use
.Fl k .
A successful request returns HTTP 200 and JSON fields
.Li stdout ,
.Li stderr
and integer
.Li status .
A nonzero command exit status still returns HTTP 200.
.It
When finished, run
.Dl relay off
in a-Shell to stop accepting requests and disable autostart.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
Use trusted networks.
Relay commands have the app's file and network access, including access to
credential files in its sandbox.
Relay is not a restricted shell.
.Pp
With
.Li mutualTLS
false, omit curl's
.Fl -cert
and
.Fl -key
options.
Anyone who can reach the port and obtain the token can then execute commands.
In this mode, the curl command printed by
.Cm status
contains the literal token.
Use the
.Ev RELAY_TOKEN
variable as in the example above to avoid saving the token in shell history.
.Pp
There is no execution timeout or client cancellation.
Avoid interactive or unbounded commands: a long-running command occupies the
serial queue.
Disconnecting the client or stopping relay does not undo its side effects.
If either output stream exceeds 8 MiB, relay discards both streams, requests
cancellation and returns HTTP 413.
If a command ignores cancellation and write errors, new requests can receive
HTTP 503; restart the app to recover.
.Pp
If the server identity is replaced, copy and trust the new public certificate
on the Mac before reconnecting.
.Sh FILES
All phone files below are in
.Pa ~/Documents/ .
.Bl -tag -width .relay-client-ca.der
.It Pa .relay.json
Configuration and token.
Keep private.
.It Pa .relay-client-ca.der
Enrolled public client CA certificate, required for mutual TLS.
.It Pa .relay-identity.p12
Private server identity.
Do not export.
.It Pa .relay-cert.pem
Public server certificate to copy to the Mac over a trusted channel.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Invalid arguments return 2.
Configuration or startup errors return 1.
